id: pm-gh1366
title: "GH-1366: Agent UX: --output-format json emits human errors while --json emits structured errors"
description: "Reported agent-facing contract defect imported from https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1366. Preserve existing shipped foundations. Detailed source observations are dated 2026-09-30 and must be revalidated before implementation."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: gh-1366,github-intake,sdk-first
created_at: "2026-10-02T17:09:19.200Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-03T18:25:04.159Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-03T18:19:33.634Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-03T18:19:33.634Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Matrix: `--json`, `--output-format json`, `--output-format=json`, supported aliases, and supported default/config modes; Matrix: success, item-not-found, invalid value, unknown flag, missing argument and policy refusal; Every JSON error stream parses as one JSON value and includes the unchanged typed code/exit status; Flags before/after command and conflicting-format precedence are deterministic; Human/TOON diagnostic paths retain their intended behavior"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "One shared SDK bootstrap resolver governs equivalent JSON selectors and explicit TOON precedence for normal parser/validation diagnostics and the executable project-runtime boundary. Repeated format flags and the terminator retain the SDK contract; warnings, refusal codes, exit status and tracker preservation are verified through real isolated pinned-project CLI processes."
expected_result: "Equivalent JSON selectors and explicit TOON precedence must apply consistently to ordinary diagnostics and early project-runtime warnings/refusals, preserving typed codes, exit status, stdout/stderr channels and persisted tracker contents."
actual_result: "Round-six shared SDK format-resolver correction: nine pre-fix precedence controls and two additional failed-before stale-warning/error stream contracts now pass. Real pinned-project executable refuses all mutation selector cases with exit 4, empty stdout and requested JSON/text stderr; persisted inventory remains unchanged. Failed stale reads emit one typed JSON value, successful reads retain their structured warning and text warnings retain their original presentation. Full current Node24.21 isolated suite passes 9648 tests with two Windows-only Linux skips; exact coverage 100/100/100/100 and zero uncovered counts (66553/66553 statements, 50904/50904 branches, 13749/13749 functions, 63454/63454 lines). All four TypeScript targets, all non-performance static stages with unchanged bounds, native non-overlapping linked suites, 124 packed Node/Bun commands with both histories verified, and nine npx/bunx workflows plus typed SDK consumers pass. All 33 changed source functions have behavior-specific documentation. Required Sentry/telemetry gate passes with zero blocking issues, 1.41 percent finish error rate and zero missing error-code rows. Interim tracker acceptance and lint refusals remain recorded with their unchanged successful reruns. A census status citation caused one prose-edge gap; its latest projection was corrected natively without inventing a dependency and history is preserved. Overlapping verification also produced a 120-second linked integration timeout and one mutation timeout; both failed receipts are retained and unchanged sequential reruns are required. Latest local SDK import-cost samples fail on Node26/24.21 while all eleven SDK bundles are byte-identical to the preceding validated phase; failed samples are retained and The local CLI transport gate also refused six wall-time bounds; both local performance failures remain explicit and exact-head hosted performance admission remains required. PR1376 exact-head hosted review/checks and merge remain required; earlier v2026.10.3 publication and broader semantic graph/docstring/platform-nightly programmes remain separate."
